# exchange.py -- the "khelo" family multi-ID exchange bet bot.
#
#   khelo24bet7.com   khelosports77.com   kheloexch99.com   khelostar247.com
#
# These four run ONE platform: the same jeetwin exchange template
# playinmatch runs, served through its DESKTOP routes (/ex/d/...) instead
# of its mobile ones. That is a third route family, so it needed a third
# adapter -- Khelo24Site in exchange_sites.py. It was NOT assumed from the
# family resemblance: the probe tested both known platforms' tells first
# and the sites answered neither (/exchange/cricket-exchange AND
# /mobile/sports both 404). See the class docstring for the full map.
#
# ── THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE FOR FOUR INSTANCES ──
# Copy it once per site. Each one is a SEPARATE PROCESS and needs its own
# EXCHANGE_BOT_TOKEN, its own ADMINS_FILE and its own accounts tab:
#
#   cp .env.khelo.exchange.example .env.khelo24bet.exchange
#   cp .env.khelo.exchange.example .env.khelosports.exchange
#   cp .env.khelo.exchange.example .env.kheloexch.exchange
#   cp .env.khelo.exchange.example .env.khelostar.exchange
#
# then edit the three marked ⬅ lines in each, and run:
#   .venv/bin/python exchange.py --env .env.<name>.exchange
#
# Two processes must never share an admins file or an accounts tab -- the
# admins file is read at import and rewritten wholesale, and the bot writes
# each ID's balance into column C of its tab, so sharing either would have
# the two clobber each other.

# ── Per-instance: change these three ──
# Telegram bot token from @BotFather -- a NEW bot per instance.
EXCHANGE_BOT_TOKEN=                                                  # ⬅
# The site this instance drives. One of the four above.
EXCHANGE_SITE_URL=https://khelo24bet7.com                            # ⬅
# Persisted admin list written by /addadmin and /removeadmin. MUST be
# distinct per instance (matches the admins.*.json gitignore rule).
ADMINS_FILE=admins.exchange.khelo24bet.json                          # ⬅

# Shown in /start; defaults to the hostname if unset.
# EXCHANGE_SITE_NAME=khelo24bet

# Comma/space-separated Telegram user IDs that may run the bot. Not
# changeable from inside the bot, only here (+ restart).
MASTER_ADMIN_ID=6936428138,1250201381

# ── Accounts sheet ──
# Row 1 = header, row 2+ = USERNAME | PASSWORD. The bot writes each ID's
# balance into column C, so GIVE EACH INSTANCE ITS OWN TAB -- a tab another
# script already writes (balance_checker.py writes column C too) would have
# the two processes overwrite each other.
EXCHANGE_SHEET_ID=
# The gid straight out of the sheet URL (…/edit?gid=1162463240). Set, it
# wins over the name and survives the tab being renamed.
EXCHANGE_WORKSHEET_GID=
# Or by title.
# EXCHANGE_WORKSHEET_NAME=EXCHANGE IDS
# Service account JSON (gitignored); share the sheet with its client_email
# as Editor -- the bot writes balances back.
SHEET_CREDENTIALS_FILE=service_account.json

# ── Proxies ──
# One proxy per line, host:port or host:port:user:pass (gitignored list).
# Accounts are handed proxies round-robin at login.
#
# Checked 2026-11-03: these sites answered a plain request from both a
# residential IP and the VPS's own datacenter IP, so a proxy is NOT
# required today the way it is for playinmatch. Two caveats:
#
#   1. The pages load AWS WAF's challenge.js, so the same behavioural wall
#      every jeetwin-family site here can raise is present -- it simply was
#      not triggered. If page GETs start answering 202/405 with an
#      `x-amzn-waf-action` header, that is it, and the fix is more exit
#      IPs (see CLAUDE.md section 2).
#   2. khelostar247.com additionally sits behind a CLOUDFLARE managed
#      challenge ("Just a moment…", cf-mitigated: challenge) which a plain
#      requests.Session cannot pass at all. That is not the AWS WAF and
#      CapSolver's AntiAwsWaf task does not apply. Until that is solved,
#      that one site is not drivable headlessly.
#
# ⚠️ The DataImpulse gateway in proxies.txt was DEAD when last checked
# (2026-11-03, from both this laptop and the VPS: ProxyError on every
# request, including a bare ipify call). Leave this unset rather than
# pointing at a dead proxy -- an unreachable proxy fails every login and
# looks exactly like wrong credentials.
# EXCHANGE_PROXY_FILE=proxies.txt

# Parallel workers. Used for BOTH bet placement and the login sweep at
# startup and on /relogin. No login rate block has been observed on this
# platform yet, but it has also never been driven with a real account, so
# start conservative and raise it once a sweep is known clean.
EXCHANGE_BET_CONCURRENCY=2

# ── Site rules ──
# Read out of these sites' own betslip JS 2026-11-03: the stake box carries
# min 2000, and odds >= 5 are refused client-side with "Sorry the bet
# cannot be accepted by our risk management team". Same numbers as both
# sibling platforms.
#
# EXCHANGE_MIN_STAKE=0 means "no client-side minimum -- let the server
# decide". Smaller stakes are accepted in practice on this family
# (operator, 2026-10-22), so copying the JS number here only blocks bets
# the site would have taken. The server is the authority either way: it
# names its own figure when it refuses one.
EXCHANGE_MIN_STAKE=0
EXCHANGE_MIN_ODDS=1.01
EXCHANGE_MAX_ODDS=5.0

# Live odds provider. Every site in this family builds its getMarketBook
# URL against khelo24bet7's host -- read off each site's own page, not
# assumed -- so this default is shared and normally stays unset.
# (The ajax.gamerstechnologies.com alternative in the same JS function sits
# behind `if ("" == 1)`, which is never true: dead code, not a fallback.)
# EXCHANGE_ODDS_HOST=https://odds4.khelo24bet7.com

# ── Before any multi-ID bet ──
# NOTHING on this platform has been driven with a real account. Verified
# anonymously: the match list, the event page, its markets and runners, the
# limit blob and the live odds book -- all through the bot's own adapter.
# Coded from the sites' own inline JS but NEVER RUN: login, balance, open
# bets, placeBet, cancel.
#
#   1. .venv/bin/python probe_khelo.py --url <site> --user <id> --pass <pw>
#      (read-only; exercises login, balance and the open-bets panel)
#   2. then the confirm screen's 🧪 Test 1 ID: an unmatched BACK @1.01 on
#      one account, cancelled immediately. Nothing can match at 1.01 (that
#      would need a lay priced at or below it), so it proves
#      place -> list -> cancel with zero exposure.
#
# Same gate khelstake, starexch, playinmatch and cricmatch each went
# through. One extra thing to watch here, because this platform differs:
# open bets are listed PER MARKET (/ex/d/api/getOpenBets/<marketId>), so
# /cancelall only sees markets the running process has opened. Confirm the
# test bet really does disappear from the site's own open-bets panel.
